      termsTitle:'Koneksyon Ambassador Terms', termsEffective:'Effective October 28, 2026 · Version 2026-10-28-v1',
      termsIntro:'These terms govern participation in the Koneksyon Ambassador Program. By applying, you confirm that you are at least 18 and agree to follow these rules.',
      t1Title:'1. Approval and eligibility', t1Body:'Applying does not guarantee acceptance. Koneksyon may approve, reject, suspend, or terminate ambassador access. Ambassadors are independent participants and are not employees of Zanara Labs LLC or Koneksyon.',
      t2Title:'2. What counts as a qualified referral', t2Body:'A qualified referral must be a new Koneksyon user who came through your assigned referral link or QR code, completed registration, passed required approval or verification, and was accepted as a legitimate unique account. Existing Koneksyon users, duplicate accounts, fake accounts, incomplete registrations, rejected accounts, self-referrals, or fraudulent activity do not count.',
      t3Title:'3. Referral and promotion rules', t3Body:'Do not create or coordinate fake accounts, reuse devices to manufacture referrals, buy fraudulent registrations, use bots, spam people, make false claims, impersonate Koneksyon, or misrepresent campaign rewards. Promotion must follow applicable laws, platform rules, Koneksyon policies, and any campaign instructions.',
      t4Title:'4. Compensation and the 100-user threshold', t4Body:'Your campaign dashboard shows your target, reward, and effective rate per qualified user. No payout is released until you reach at least 100 qualified users. If you have fewer than 100, eligible activity rolls forward. After the threshold is reached, eligible unpaid referrals are processed in 14-day payout periods. If a campaign ends, remaining legitimate unpaid referrals may be included in a final payout after review.',
      t5Title:'5. U.S. dollar payout methods', t5Body:'All amounts are denominated in U.S. dollars. Supported methods are Cash App, Zelle, MoneyGram, and USD bank transfer to a USD-denominated account at Unibank, Capital Bank, Banque de L’Union Haitienne, Sogebel, or Sogebank. You must provide accurate payment information. Provider, intermediary, or receiving-bank fees may apply.',
      t6Title:'6. Review, holds, and fraud', t6Body:'Koneksyon may review referrals before or after they are counted and may hold, reject, reverse, or remove referrals or payouts connected to duplicates, abuse, bans, fabricated registrations, suspicious device activity, or other fraud. Only server-validated qualified referrals are payable.',
